  "rules": "Two cipher alphabets: GP order for A, reversed GP order for B. Canonical plaintext index P=(rank_active(C)+sign*K_active[counter])mod29. Each key has its own counter. All ciphertext runes are decoded, including F. On ciphertext F, hold the selected key counter; otherwise advance it. Policy key-only toggles alphabet after every rune. Policy both holds alphabet on F and toggles otherwise. Non-runes do not advance state. Page-local reset. Encryption computes C from current state and P, then updates state from the resulting C, so marker handling is deterministic.",
